  "notes": "**pixel-press** — local-first video compression for the web. Nothing uploads; everything runs on your machine.\n\nFirst launch downloads FFmpeg/FFprobe and (optionally) a ~270 MB on-device LLM — SHA-256-verified, installed into your app data directory. The app then works fully offline. No accounts, no telemetry.\n\n> Ad-hoc signed for Apple Silicon (no Developer ID yet) — macOS Gatekeeper still blocks on first open: right-click → Open, or System Settings → Privacy & Security → Open Anyway.\n\n| Platform | Asset | Requirements |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| macOS Apple Silicon | `*_aarch64.dmg` | macOS 11+ on Apple Silicon |\n| macOS Intel | `*_x64.dmg` | macOS 10.15+ on Intel |\n| Linux x64 | `*_amd64.AppImage` or `*_amd64.deb` | glibc ≥ 2.31, WebKitGTK 4.1 |\n| Linux ARM64 | `*_arm64.AppImage` or `*_arm64.deb` | Raspberry Pi OS / Ubuntu ARM64 |\n\n`setup-manifest.json` lists SHA-256 + size + source for the FFmpeg/FFprobe/LLM artifacts downloaded on first launch.\n\npixel-press is MIT-licensed. FFmpeg/FFprobe are separate GPL/LGPL binaries downloaded by you at first launch; LLM weights (SmolLM2-360M, Apache-2.0) likewise. See `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`.\n\n> **Flavors:** tags containing `-dev` (e.g. `v0.1.0-dev`) produce the development flavor — **\"pixel-press Dev\"** (`com.pixelpress.app.dev`) — marked as a prerelease. It installs side-by-side with production and never overrides it. Plain tags produce the production build.",
